534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446370 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446370 1077 "selection" 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446370 1078 #edb/ref 17592186446340 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446370 1079 #uuid "fb932edd-7a39-5566-85fa-5d17f1b76d5d" 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446371 1068 #edb/ref 17592186446361 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446371 1069 "q-141201" 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446371 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446371 1071 "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and  $\\text{rank}(A)=4?$ \n\nI. $A$ is invertible\n\nII. $\\text{Col}(A)=\\{0\\}$\n\nIII. $\\text{nullity}(A)=0$" 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446371 1072 #uuid "007b2eff-be4f-5ff5-af75-29d7ce49d108" 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446371 1074 "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=4=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn. \n\n- Statement I is true. By the invertible matrix theorem,  $A$ is an invertible matrix because $\\text{rank}(A)=4.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $A$ is invertible, it must be $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4}.$\n\n- Statement III is true. By the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{nullity}(A)=0$ because $A$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is, \"I and III only.\"" 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446372 1068 #edb/ref 17592186446365 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446372 1069 "q-34929" 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446372 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446372 1071 "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and $v=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ is a solution of the equation $Ax=0?$\n\nI. $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0$\n\nII. $A$ is invertible\n\nIII. $\\text{rank}(A)=4$" 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446372 1072 #uuid "0a0c9232-89fc-57dc-83d9-632995f2a765" 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446372 1074 "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=4=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn. \n\n- Statement I is true. Since $v\\ne 0$ and $Av=0,$ \nthen $v\\in \\text{Null}(A)$ and, therefore, $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0,$ then according to the invertible matrix theorem, the matrix $A$ can't be invertible.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ is not invertible, then by the invertible matrix theorem, we must have $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446373 1068 #edb/ref 17592186446363 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446373 1069 "q-141348" 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446373 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446373 1071 "$$\nA\\text{ is invertible}\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\bbox[3pt,white,border: 2px solid Gainsboro]{\\phantom{WW}}={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the equivalence above, where $A$ is an $n\\,\\times \\,n$ matrix. Which of the following should be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?" 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446373 1072 #uuid "20d9e520-65af-5666-8bc0-5f07c585e966" 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446373 1074 "Recall that the *invertible matrix theorem* states the following: \n\n*Let $A$ be an $n\\,\\times \\,n$ matrix. Then we have the following equivalence:*\n\n$$\nA\\text{ is invertible}\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is $\\text{Col}(A).$" 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446374 1068 #edb/ref 17592186446368 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446374 1069 "q-141198" 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446374 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446374 1071 "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and  $det(A)=0?$ \n\nI. $A$ is not invertible\n\nII. $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 5$\n\nIII. $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}$" 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446374 1072 #uuid "40fb1ecb-b40f-5f25-b77a-57f70d15c44b" 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446374 1074 "Since $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{5} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col)}(A)=5=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null)}(A)=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn. \n\n- Statement I is true. A matrix $A$ is invertible if and only if $det(A)\\ne 0.$ Since here we have $det(A)=0,$ our matrix $A$ is not invertible.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, by the invertible matrix theorem\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\text{rank}(A)=5.$\nSince $A$ is not invertible, we must have $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 5.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ is not invertible,  it must be $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne \\{0\\}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446375 1068 #edb/ref 17592186446364 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446375 1069 "q-141196" 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446375 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446375 1071 "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{1} \\\\ 2{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,|\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R\\}?\n$$\n\nI. $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0$\n\nII. $A$ is invertible\n\nIII. $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4}$" 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446375 1072 #uuid "66aeec20-f33b-58e9-909c-e866d7b79c69" 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446375 1074 "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=4=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Since \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\,|\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R\\}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=2\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0,$ then according to the invertible matrix theorem, the matrix $A$ can't be invertible.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ is not invertible, then by the invertible matrix theorem, we must have $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne {R}^{4}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446376 1068 #edb/ref 17592186446366 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446376 1069 "q-141345" 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446376 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446376 1071 "$$\nA\\text{ is invertible}\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\bbox[3pt,white,border: 2px solid Gainsboro]{\\phantom{WW}}=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the equivalence above, where $A$ is an $n\\,\\times \\,n$ matrix. Which of the following should be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?" 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446376 1072 #uuid "783f1132-a5b8-51d7-9eb1-23f2ac5cdb40" 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446376 1074 "Recall that the *invertible matrix theorem* states the following: \n\n*Let $A$ be an $n\\,\\times \\,n$ matrix. Then we have the following equivalence:*\n\n$$\nA\\text{ is invertible}\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is $\\text{Null}(A).$" 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446377 1068 #edb/ref 17592186446369 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446377 1069 "q-141215" 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446377 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446377 1071 "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $\\text{__________}$ .*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $det(A)=0$\n\nII. $\\text{Null}(A)={R}^{6}$\n\nIII. $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=6$" 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446377 1072 #uuid "833e6fc8-0df5-5faa-ab1e-b5f4126e71c3" 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446377 1074 "If $A$ is an $6\\times 6$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{6} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=6=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $det(A)=0$* $\\,\\times $ \n\nSince the matrix $A$ is invertible, it must be  $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then  $\\text{Null}(A)={R}^{6}.$* $\\,\\times $\n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem,  we have $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=6.$* $\\,✓$ \n\nSince $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=6.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446378 1068 #edb/ref 17592186446362 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446378 1069 "q-142479" 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446378 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446378 1071 "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{rank}(A)<n,$ then $\\text{__________}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $A$ is invertible\n\nII. $\\text{Null}(A)$ has no basis\n\nIII. $det(A)=0$" 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446378 1072 #uuid "a9326523-4bce-5554-9699-fb91223b9531" 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446378 1074 "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{rank}(A)<n,$ then  $A$ is invertible.* $\\,\\times $ \n\nSince $\\text{rank}(A)<n,$  then according to the invertible matrix theorem, $A$ can't be invertible.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{rank}(A)<n,$ then  $\\text{Null}(A)$ has no basis.* $\\,\\times $\n\nIndeed, since $A$ is *not* invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0,$ which means that $\\text{Null}(A)$ actually has a basis.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{rank}(A)<n,$ then  $det(A)=0.$* $\\,✓$  \n\nIndeed, since $A$ is not invertible it must be $det(A)=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446379 1068 #edb/ref 17592186446367 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446379 1069 "q-141194" 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446379 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446379 1071 "$$\nA\\text{ is invertible}\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\bbox[3pt,white,border: 2px solid Gainsboro]{\\phantom{W}} \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the equivalence above, where $A$ is an $n\\,\\times \\,n$ matrix. Which of the following should be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?" 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446379 1072 #uuid "e7063fa7-cfd5-5cea-b242-ca27bb233616" 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446379 1074 "Recall that the *invertible matrix theorem* states the following: \n\n*Let $A$ be an $n\\,\\times \\,n$ matrix. Then we have the following equivalence:*\n\n$$\nA\\text{ is invertible}\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is $\\text{rank}(A).$" 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446380 1068 #edb/ref 17592186446370 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446380 1069 "q-141341" 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446380 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446380 1071 "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then  $\\text{__________}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $A$ is invertible\n\nII. $det(A)=0$\n\nIII. $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=n$" 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446380 1072 #uuid "ec73c900-b909-5aa7-beeb-5f5b6ee2fba4" 13194139534974 17592186045417 true] [17592186446380 1074 "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $A$ is invertible.* $\\,✓$\n\nIndeed, by the invertible matrix theorem, since $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ we must have that $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $det(A)=0.$* $\\,\\times $ \n\nSince $A$ is invertible, then we must have $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\text{nullity}(A)=0,$ then $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=n.$ * $\\,✓$\n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=n.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" 13194139534974 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-001907a0-d758-52f3-b5d8-ac5e8cf1f77e" 17592186446311 "answer-07ea5ae9-a33a-5951-9b11-5dc1678ec0ec" 17592186446312 "answer-0d49a551-9ec5-52ad-a34a-89d55b7486b5" 17592186446313 "answer-22d4c374-6702-575a-adef-908f42b74c37" 17592186446314 "answer-2487a691-60de-5d0e-a46b-689f90f253ca" 17592186446315 "answer-2557bc60-0ebd-5724-813e-5497b927e3ef" 17592186446316 "answer-2dee1bb0-b584-5a13-acb7-dbc8b8f98b95" 17592186446317 "answer-3307d8dd-316e-59b9-a236-3cf5704a1eda" 17592186446318 "answer-41750c54-9a68-5140-acec-016759823bad" 17592186446319 "answer-53b34189-99d5-5baf-aa84-89f8e9508140" 17592186446320 "answer-5602a65b-5713-5ed2-bdd4-7c2a89efe1f3" 17592186446321 "answer-5962da19-877d-530f-b40f-aae8873a783f" 17592186446322 "answer-5ab377df-73df-53f2-81bc-0c28114d3720" 17592186446323 "answer-5fb3aa43-1e84-516c-8972-6a71a1a76857" 17592186446324 "answer-6358e671-90b3-5914-a718-8213a1f17a31" 17592186446325 "answer-65a82f6c-7a03-5152-b67b-6b75c8f2f8df" 17592186446326 "answer-662ea6db-c29f-5f39-b454-f93e28a4789e" 17592186446327 "answer-6866f740-c6c6-5a04-9ec8-25e5e19817c8" 17592186446328 "answer-6a0d3e4b-0e93-59fe-9cf9-ff2f7de1a3e7" 17592186446329 "answer-720f0040-8787-5886-9c1c-402554299b56" 17592186446330 "answer-75e28f10-a377-5525-ba66-0cdc4c8e054e" 17592186446331 "answer-76cde27a-9ace-54a5-8396-92267ce3cc46" 17592186446332 "answer-83819081-3ffe-5b21-ac5b-ef6bd26bb168" 17592186446333 "answer-8385037e-b7cf-5ce8-80e7-5480da9f4742" 17592186446334 "answer-86f2e9f4-3420-54d6-a57c-2966d7bea624" 17592186446335 "answer-8d75866b-a6fe-5c0e-8c96-11f1e0e723da" 17592186446336 "answer-9a43c232-d1ff-5d5b-967a-f97c5c62802c" 17592186446337 "answer-9adf27f7-10ea-578a-a1d6-83396d7db9c6" 17592186446338 "answer-a01f5c26-889c-59f3-aea4-5b800234178a" 17592186446339 "answer-a1868d1e-